('The Mystery of the Blue Train', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Mystery_of_the_Blue_Train-Agatha_Christie-67b83-339808.jpg', 'Agatha Christie', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books: Mystery, Detective, Horror, Thriller, Fantasy and Adventure', '9780008129484', 'English', 316, '1st Edition, 2017', 528.0, 528, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'The daughter of an American millionaire dies on a train en route for Nice…When the luxurious Blue Train arrives at Nice, a guard attempts to wake serene Ruth Kettering from her slumbers. But she will never wake again – for a heavy blow has killed her, disfiguring her features almost beyond recognition. What is more, her precious rubies are missing.The prime suspect is Ruth’s estranged husband, Derek. Yet Poirot is not convinced, so he stages an eerie re-enactment of the journey, complete with the murderer on board…'),
('Destination Unknown', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/Destination_Unknown-Agatha_Christie-53b6a-340143.jpg', 'Agatha Christie', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9780008196363', 'English', 256, '1st Edition, 2017', 512.0, 512, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'A young woman with nothing to live for is persuaded to embark on a suicide mission to find a missing scientist…When a number of leading scientists disappear without trace, concern grows within the international intelligence community. Are they being kidnapped? Blackmailed?Brainwashed?One woman appears to have the key to the mystery. Unfortunately, Olive Betteron now lies in a hospital bed, dying from injuries sustained in a Moroccan plane crash. Meanwhile, in a Casablanca hotel room, Hilary Craven prepares to take her own life. But her suicide attempt is about to be interrupted by a man who will offer her an altogether more thrilling way to die…'),
('The Unexpected Guest', 'https://rokbucket.rokomari.io/ProductNew20190903/260X372/The_Unexpected_Guest-Agatha_Christie-72e4d-340176.jpg', 'Agatha Christie', 'Harpercollins publishers (India)', 'Foreign Language Books', '9780008196677', 'English', 176, '1st Edition, 2017', 504.0, 504, '65% Off', NULL, 5, 'Pre-Order', 'A young man, broken down in the fog, witnesses a murder he is asked to conceal